  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Abdel Shafi Community Health Association</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ACHA will rehabilitate, equip, and operationalise ACHA&#x2019;s existing Women and Girls Safe Space in the Najat Centre to enhance the provision of GBV-SRHR services. The Centre is a functioning One-Stop Centre (OSC), specializing in reproductive, psychological, and social support.The project will scale up the built-in feedback and complaints mechanism, including safe channels for PSEA complaints within the OSC, and will train staff on their use. In addition, policies and protocols for youth protection will be developed, with corresponding staff training to ensure effective implementation.Multi-sectoral GBV-SRHR services will be provided for women, girls, and adolescents/youth through the OSC and safe spaces. ACHA will also deploy mobile clinic teams to reach hard-to-access and vulnerable areas in northern Gaza, building on its existing mobile outreach capacity and long-standing experience within these communities.Further, ACHA will conduct training for service providers on the service referral directory and ensure its dissemination for effectiveuse. Youth-led initiatives will be implemented to promote GBV prevention and response, and to improve access to reliable SRHR information and services.Lastly, awareness-raising sessions will be conducted for adolescentgirls, youth, men, and boys on their rights, PSEA, SRHR, and GBV protection mechanisms</narrative>
  </description>
